From 3770b2280282e01eddcba6404cab98d1cf681ed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:53:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 276/283] feat(qwen35): compose public composites from shared
 sub-composites

Add the private _compose_program primitive: a checked, dead-code-free IR
splice of a sub-program's pure dataflow with parameter binding (CoreType
checked) and longest-prefix SSA renaming.  Composition consumes a child
composite's FP32 internal value so no bf16 round-trip or extra cast is
introduced.

Reuse public composites in the large builders and in the executable graph:

* build_qwen35_position_control <- position_ids + causal_mask_from_positions
* build_qwen35_gated_delta_conv_state <- causal_conv1d_state
* build_decoder_subgraph <- rms_norm + swiglu
* build_qwen35_attention_kv_cache <- gqa_repeat_kv x2 + batched_matmul x2
  + causal_mask + stable_softmax
* build_attention_subgraph <- rope_rotate_half + causal_mask
  + stable_softmax + gqa_repeat_kv
* build_qwen35_text_decoder_graph reuses position_control at the top and,
  per layer, rms_norm / rope_rotate_half / batched_matmul / causal_mask /
  stable_softmax (full attention) and causal_conv1d_state / l2_norm (GDR)

Every public signature is unchanged and every CoreProgram.canonical_json()
is byte-identical to the pre-refactor snapshot; the frozen bf16 graph digest
66dd40770dbb41251f0f7ec9b15b75b604daddc95633aabc24d9e48ffff33c6d is kept.
Add test_qwen35_composite_composition.py: exact structural embedding
assertions for each composition edge plus frozen canonical digest pins.

(cherry picked from commit 54d2f4ea984468579689c893eced95cc90783ba6)
